cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Terraflux in your work, please cite it as below, and cite the papers of the methods you used (see https://sacridini.github.io/terraflux/about/citing/)."
type: software
title: "Terraflux: landscape ecology and land change modelling from a laptop to a cluster"
abstract: >-
  Terraflux is a free, open-source desktop application and command line for landscape ecology: habitat patterns,
  landscape metrics, connectivity, spatial prioritization, species distributions and land use change simulation,
  with the same results as the reference tools, from a laptop to a cluster.
authors:
  - family-names: Lacerda
    given-names: Eduardo
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0003-3803-5842"
version: 1.67.0
date-released: 2026-11-24
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.24515275
identifiers:
  - type: doi
    value: 10.5281/zenodo.24515275
    description: "The concept DOI of Terraflux on Zenodo: it resolves to the latest version, and each version has its own DOI."
license: GPL-3.0-or-later
repository-code: "https://github.com/sacridini/terraflux"
url: "https://sacridini.github.io/terraflux/"
keywords:
  - landscape ecology
  - land use and land cover change
  - conservation planning
  - habitat connectivity
  - landscape metrics
  - species distribution modelling
  - spatial prioritization
  - raster analysis
